# decimal_exact_money — exact money arithmetic via Decimal (README §27/§30.5,
# X-093). Money/Decimal is a scaled Int64 (scale 2: the raw value is amount*100),
# so $10.50 + $5.25 = $15.75 is computed EXACTLY as 1050 + 525 = 1575 with
# `decimal.add` — no binary-float rounding error. (Float money is rejected by the
# gate; Decimal is the accepted exact form.)
#
# Correctness observation: 1050 + 525 == 1575 ($10.50 + $5.25 = $15.75).
# Expected output: PASS lines + `---- 2 passed, 0 failed ----`

DecimalExactMoney is project
DecimalExactMoney module examplesDecimalExactMoney
DecimalExactMoney target console
DecimalExactMoney entry main

examplesDecimalExactMoney is module
examplesDecimalExactMoney path examples.decimalExactMoney
examplesDecimalExactMoney exports main
examplesDecimalExactMoney purpose "Add two money amounts exactly with Decimal"
examplesDecimalExactMoney invariant "Scaled-integer money adds without float error"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32

Decimal is alias
Decimal for Int64
Decimal purpose "Fixed-scale money: the raw Int64 is the amount * 100 (scale 2)"

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap no
main async no
main purpose "Compute $10.50 + $5.25 exactly and assert $15.75"
main invariant "Writes the test harness summary"
main let priceA immutable Decimal 1050
main let priceB immutable Decimal 525
main let harnessName immutable String "decimal_exact_money"
main let harnessExpected immutable Decimal 1575
main let noopDecoy immutable Decimal 0
main let noopName immutable String "decimal_exact_money: real sum (not the no-op 0)"
main do addPrices
main do writeResult
main do noopCheck
main do harnessReport
main return harnessSummaryCode

addPrices is call
addPrices in main
addPrices invokes decimal.add
addPrices arg left Decimal priceA
addPrices arg right Decimal priceB
addPrices out total Decimal

writeResult is call
writeResult in main
writeResult invokes test.assertEqualInt64
writeResult arg name String harnessName
writeResult arg expected Int64 harnessExpected
writeResult arg actual Int64 total

noopCheck is call
noopCheck in main
noopCheck invokes test.assertNotEqualInt64
noopCheck arg name String noopName
noopCheck arg expected Int64 noopDecoy
noopCheck arg actual Int64 total

harnessReport is call
harnessReport in main
harnessReport invokes test.summary
harnessReport out harnessSummaryCode ExitCode
